# v0 UI boundary

The founder uses v0 for visible UI/UX generation. Treat v0 output as a user-supplied UI artifact, not as product authority.

- Do not independently redesign final visual UI when a v0 design/export exists.
- Cursor owns Rust core, typed authority/API contracts, local IPC, client bindings, deterministic fixtures, accessibility, tests, packaging, and privacy qualification.
- UI never directly owns or opens canonical storage, keys, unrestricted filesystem, model/network authority, or external actions.
- Do not inherit Next.js/Vercel/server/database/network assumptions from v0 unless an owning MedScale spec explicitly admits them.
- Use synthetic/non-PHI data in v0 prompts, screenshots, previews, fixtures, and tests.
- Integrate v0 through `imports/v0/` provenance and `docs/planning/V0_UI_INTEGRATION_CONTRACT.md`.
- If Tauri/WebView privacy qualification fails, preserve the v0 visual/component intent while moving to a safer shell; never weaken privacy to preserve a framework.